  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\Delta T_f=i K_f m \\\\ & 0.558=i \\times 1.86 \\times 0.1 \\\\ & i=\\frac{0.558}{0.186}=3\\end{aligned}$\nNumber of ions when 100\\% ionisation takes place $=3$\n$\\left[\\mathrm{Cr}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_5 \\mathrm{Cl}\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}_2 \\xrightarrow{\\text { aqueous solution }}\\left[\\mathrm{Cr}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_5 \\mathrm{Cl}^{2+}\\right]^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$\nNumber of ions $=3$",
    "image": null
  },
